## notes
input_fail=76 of 22,075 inbound frames (0.34%); the drops are concentrated in the
opening seconds (45 by frame 654, 55 by 1223, 76 by the end), i.e. the phone bursts
its initial window and 64 slots still reject part of that burst. overlap grew to 155
by the end of the opening burst, so the phone did retransmit. Steady state reached
about 560 frames/s (~0.9 MB/s in 5 s windows) after the slow start.
This run used merge OFF (-j 0), so joined frames stay 0; the 1.12 MB/s best used merge ON.
Before freezing, the chain was stopped by killing only the package children (verified: no leftovers, 49876/49877/8771/15353 free). No radio state was reset or channel changed. Note: the keep-alive TCP connection stayed open after the transfer (proxy 2 active=1, lwip_recv/local_recv), so the proxy holds those two worker threads until the phone closes it.
